From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:51:34 -0400
Subject: feat: a collapsed folder keeps a pin that is awake listed

GitHub issue 35 (folders F3; BACKLOG S-304): a collapsed folder showed
only the tab on screen, so leaving a pinned tab in it hid that tab, and
going back to it took opening the folder. Now a collapsed folder keeps
listing a Space pin that is awake under its header; asleep, the pin folds
away with the rest, and a tab that is not a pin does too. TabStripModel
takes a second embedder predicate, the tabs kept under a collapsed folder,
which SpaceModel answers for its awake pins.

Why: the owner asked for it on 2026-10-28.
Removable when: Chromium's folders grow their own rule for what a
collapsed folder keeps listed.
